  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_15_09_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <para>For questions 1 – 5, use the following scenario to graph an inequality from a table:</para>
      <para>
        <quote>Andre is making trail mix with dried fruit and mixed nuts. Dried fruit costs $3 per pound and mixed nuts cost $6 per pound. He wants to spend no more than $54 on the trail mix. The inequality \(y \leq −2x + 18\) represents the number of pounds of dried fruit, \(y\), he can buy for \(x\) pounds of nuts.</quote>
     </para>
      <!--Q#1-->
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>The related equation \(y = -2x + 18\) represents the boundary line of the inequality. Complete the table of values to find points on the boundary line of the inequality.</para>
            <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
              <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              <row>
                  <entry>0</entry>
                  <entry/>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>2</entry>
                  <entry/>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>4</entry>
                  <entry/>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>6</entry>
                  <entry/>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
              <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              <row>
                  <entry>0</entry>
                  <entry>18</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>2</entry>
                  <entry>14</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>4</entry>
                  <entry>10</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>6</entry>
                  <entry>6</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q#2-->
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Graph the data from your table of values that represents this scenario using the Desmos tool below.</item>
      </list>
      <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/><example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <!--QUESTION IS OUTSIDE OF INTERACTION DUE TO DESMOS-->
